From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: World of Warcraft <warcraft@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:22:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Destructible buildings with an invisibility of their own are
 seen only by those who detect it

A destructible building (a building as the game's own out in the world
are) is always seen, whatever detects it. One given an invisibility of its
own (mod-brill-home's Community Projects: a building that shows from a
project's stage, carried by an invisibility kind) is seen only by those
who detect it, as any other object is.
---
 src/server/game/Entities/GameObject/GameObject.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/server/game/Entities/GameObject/GameObject.cpp b/src/server/game/Entities/GameObject/GameObject.cpp
index 931d2a5fde..f6f25f93ac 100644
--- a/src/server/game/Entities/GameObject/GameObject.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/GameObject/GameObject.cpp
@@ -1250,7 +1250,8 @@ bool GameObject::IsAlwaysVisibleFor(WorldObject const* seer) const
     if (WorldObject::IsAlwaysVisibleFor(seer))
         return true;
 
-    if (IsTransport() || IsDestructibleBuilding())
+    // (a destructible building with an invisibility of its own is seen only by those who detect it)
+    if (IsTransport() || (IsDestructibleBuilding() && !m_invisibility.GetFlags()))
         return true;
 
     if (!seer)
